Chapter: IpChecksumOdd
  cites Net chapter Ethernet
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 We say:

Section: Fixtures

 witness-checksum is the independent witness and it must not be deleted as a
 duplicate of ip-checksum. It is the separately written one's-complement sum
 that was icmp-checksum in the Icmp chapter until the two were collapsed onto
 ip-checksum; it lives here so agreement between the two remains two
 implementations agreeing rather than one agreeing with itself. Anything that
 changes ip-checksum must leave this body alone.

  witness-checksum : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  witness-checksum (data) (i) (len) (sum) =
    if i >= len then
      let folded = bit-and sum 65535 + bit-shru sum 16
      in let folded2 = bit-and folded 65535 + bit-shru folded 16
      in bit-and (bit-xor folded2 65535) 65535
    else if i + 1 >= len then
      witness-checksum data (i + 1) len (sum + bit-shl (list-at data i) 8)
    else witness-checksum data (i + 2) len (sum + read-be16 data i)

  odd3 : List Integer = [1, 2, 3]
  odd5 : List Integer = [255, 1, 128, 7, 200]
  odd1 : List Integer = [171]
  even4 : List Integer = [1, 2, 3, 4]
  even20 : List Integer = [69, 0, 0, 40, 0, 0, 0, 0, 64, 6, 0, 0, 10, 0, 2, 15, 10, 0, 2, 100]

  ip-of : List Integer -> Integer
  ip-of (xs) = ip-checksum xs 0 (list-length xs) 0

  witness-of : List Integer -> Integer
  witness-of (xs) = witness-checksum xs 0 (list-length xs) 0

 Padding by hand is what a caller had to do to get the right answer before the
 odd-tail arm existed. It must now agree with the unpadded call, which is what
 says the arm does exactly the job the padding did.

  ip-padded : List Integer -> Integer
  ip-padded (xs) = ip-checksum (xs & [0]) 0 (list-length xs + 1) 0

Section: Entry
  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("odd3-agrees=" & show (ip-of odd3 == witness-of odd3))
    print-line-uni ("odd5-agrees=" & show (ip-of odd5 == witness-of odd5))
    print-line-uni ("odd1-agrees=" & show (ip-of odd1 == witness-of odd1))
    print-line-uni ("odd3-equals-padded=" & show (ip-of odd3 == ip-padded odd3))
    print-line-uni ("odd5-equals-padded=" & show (ip-of odd5 == ip-padded odd5))
    print-line-uni ("even4-agrees=" & show (ip-of even4 == witness-of even4))
    print-line-uni ("even20-agrees=" & show (ip-of even20 == witness-of even20))
    print-line-uni ("even4-value=" & show (ip-of even4))
    print-line-uni ("even20-value=" & show (ip-of even20))
    print-line-uni ("odd3-value=" & show (ip-of odd3))
    print-line-uni ("odd5-value=" & show (ip-of odd5))
  end
